        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Sulphur Bank Mine\n- Places: California, Lake County, Eastlake\n- Plants: Eriogonum nervulosum\n- Topics: mercury production\n\nFacts:\n- Sulphur Bank Mine was a business in California that operated from 1873 to 1883.\n- Sulphur Bank Mine became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.\n- Eastlake in Lake County, California, is located southwest of Sulphur Bank Mine.\n- Eriogonum nervulosum is a flowering plant found in Lake County, California.",
